	<!--  
Darkfall 2.0
Music Implementation System

1.	CATEGORIES, GROUPS & TRACKS

	The Music in Darkfall 2.0 is organized into Categories and Groups:
	
		CAT A: 	Generic Ambient Tracks (1 group)
		CAT B:	Racial Themes (6 different groups)
		CAT C:	Subcontinent Themes (4 different groups)
		CAT D:	Other Tracks
		
	______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
	Each Groups has the following attributes:
		
		“Priority” 				– 	For now all the categories have the same priority.
									If the player moves from a lower priority zone to a higher one while a track from the first (low priority) category is playing,
									then the track will fade out and a new one from the higher priority playlist will start playing. If the zones have the same priority, nothing happens.
									default value = 0

		“PauseDuration” – 	Is measured in seconds and describes the time of silence (pause) between consecutive tracks.
									
		“Loop” 				– 	Takes values of “0” or “1”. The “1” is currently used only for the Loading Screen Music group. 
										

		“Volume”				 – Takes values from "0.0" to "1.0". The main volume of the group for mixing purposes (currently not used).
										default value = 1

	______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________	
	Each Group is consisted of tracks (.ogg files). Each file has the following attributes:
		
		“Time” 							– Takes values of “Day” or “Night”. This tells the system on what time of day is the track available for play. 
													So in a category (eg. Ambient tracks) there are tracks that only play during the day and tracks that only play during the night.
													If not existent, the track playes during both day and night.

		“TimeLock” 					–	Is measured in seconds. This is a safety net that tells the system how much time MUST pass after a track has played, 
													until that track is available again. It is currently used in the Racial Themes and in the Continent Theme tracks. 
													default value = o

		“PlayFirst” 						– Takes values of “true” or “false”. This attribute tells the system if the specific track is to be played first from the current group. 
													default value = false
													
		“PlayOnlyOnTransition”	 – Takes values of “True” or “False”. This attribute tells the system that the current track should only be played if the was a Group transition involved. 
													default value = false
	
	

2.	CATEGORIES
	A.	Ambient Track. 
		
		The first Category is consisted of the Ambient Tracks Group. This is the general group that governs most of the world of Agon. 
		There are tracks that play during the day and tracks that play during the night with 30 minutes silence intervals. 
	
	B.	Racial Themes. The second Category is consisted of 6 different Groups. Each group has all of the Ambient Tracks (CAT A) plus one extra track for the specific race. So we have the following groups:
		
		1.	Human Group: CAT A traks + Human Theme.
		2.	Orc Group: CAT A tracks + Orc Theme.
		3.	Alar Group: CAT A track + Alfar Theme.
		4.	Mirdain Group: CAT A tracks + Mirdain Theme.
		5.	Mahirim Group: CAT A tracks + Mahirim Theme.
		6.	Dwarf Group: CAT A Tracks + Dwarf Theme.
	
		The Racial Themes Groups functions as follows:
	
		The race theme track will play first when the player enters a CAT B zone. When the track finishes, it won’t be heard again, unless 2 hours have passed (“TimeLock”) and the player re-enters the zone (“PlayOnlyOnTransition”=”true”). Also after the racial theme is heard, the other tracks (ambient tracks) will be drawn from the system randomly every 30 minutes. 

	C.	Subcontinent Themes. The third Category is consisted of 4 different Groups. Each group has all of the Ambient Tracks (CAT A) plus one extra track for the specific subcontinent. So we have the following groups:
	
		1.	Niflheim Group: CAT A tracks + Ice theme.
		2.	Yssam Group: CAT A tracks + Jungle theme.
		3.	Rubaiyat Group: CAT A tracks + Desert theme.
		4.	Cairn Group: CAT A tracks + Wasteland theme.
		
		This Category’s Groups function as the Racial Themes Category. The subcontinent theme track will play first when the player enters a CAT C zone. When the track finishes, it won’t be heard again, unless 2 hours have passed (“TimeLock”) and the player re-enters the zone (“PlayOnlyOnTransition”=”true”). Also after the subcontinent theme is heard, the other tracks (ambient tracks) will be drawn from the system randomly every 30 minutes.

	D.	Other Tracks. In this Category are placed all other Groups. For example Central Area, the Central Castle and the dungeon groups.
	--> 
	
